Assume Countable Choice. Let $F:\widehat K	o K$ be an admissible $C^1$ orientation-preserving cell diffeomorphism and let $u$ be $C^1$ on $K$. With $\widehat u=u\circ F$, one has $
abla_xu\circ F=DF^{-T}
abla_{\xi}\widehat u$ and $\int_K |
abla u|^2dx=\int_{\widehat K}J_F
abla\widehat u^T(DF^{-1}DF^{-T})
abla\widehat u\,d\xi$. For a regular $k$-dimensional parametrized face $f:U\subset\mathbb R^k	o\mathbb R^d$ with metric $G_f=Df^TDf$, the induced area factor is $\sqrt{\det G_f}$ and the tangential gradient of $u\circ f$ is $DfG_f^{-1}
abla(u\circ f)$; its squared norm is $
abla(u\circ f)^TG_f^{-1}
abla(u\circ f)$.

Assume the Axiom of Choice and Countable Choice. Let $\widehat\Omega=(-1,1)^2$, let $\Phi(x,y)=(x,y+x^2/4)$, and let $\Phi_h$ be its continuous piecewise-affine nodal interpolant on a shape-regular matching triangular mesh with maximum diameter $h\le1$, small enough that $J_h=\det D\Phi_h\ge1/2$ as in [[lem-parabolic-domain-map-approximation]]. Put $J=\det D\Phi$ and define the pulled-back Laplace tensors $$B=J D\Phi^{-1}D\Phi^{-T},\qquad B_h=J_hD\Phi_h^{-1}D\Phi_h^{-T}.$$ On $V=H^1_0(\widehat\Omega)$ set $$a(v,w)=\int_{\widehat\Omega}
abla v^TB
abla w,\qquad a_h(v,w)=\int_{\widehat\Omega}
abla v^TB_h
abla w.$$ Let $V_h$ be the finite-dimensional space of continuous functions on $\overline{\widehat\Omega}$ that are affine on each triangle and vanish on $\partial\widehat\Omega$, viewed as a subspace of $V$. Suppose $a$ and $a_h$ are uniformly bounded and coercive on $V$ and $V_h$, respectively, with constants independent of $h$, $F\in V^*$ and $F_h\in V_h^*$ are bounded, $u\in H^2(\widehat\Omega)\cap V$ is real-valued and satisfies $a(u,w)=F(w)$ for every $w\in V$, and $u_h\in V_h$ satisfies $a_h(u_h,w_h)=F_h(w_h)$ for every $w_h\in V_h$. If a common physical boundary lift $G\in C^2$ with bounded first and second derivatives on a convex neighborhood of the two geometry images is used, let $\ell_{\partial,h}$ be its pulled-back residual from [[lem-curved-boundary-lift-residual]] and set $\epsilon_{\partial,h}=\|\ell_{\partial,h}\|_{V^*}$. Assume the load difference on $V_h$ splits as $$ (F-F_h)|_{V_h}=L_{\mathrm{bulk},h}+\ell_{\partial,h}|_{V_h},\qquad \|L_{\mathrm{bulk},h}\|_{V_h^*}\le\epsilon_{F,h}^{\mathrm{bulk}},\qquad \epsilon_{F,h}^{\mathrm{bulk}}\ge0.$$ Here the $V^*$ and $V_h^*$ norms are induced by the $H^1$ norm. If no lift is used, set $\ell_{\partial,h}=0$ and take the same bound for the full load difference. Then $$\|u-u_h\|_{H^1(\widehat\Omega)}\le C igl(h\|u\|_{H^2(\widehat\Omega)}+\epsilon_{F,h}^{\mathrm{bulk}}+\epsilon_{\partial,h} igr).$$ where $C$ is independent of $h$. For the parabolic geometry family, $\epsilon_{\partial,h}\le C_G(e_0+e_1)\le C_Gh$.
